    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch12-13: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.81";
    dc:description "The closeness prediction is explicit and can be tested with phylogenetic clustering. Existing coverage is strong for well-studied archipelagos but insufficient for the full taxonomic scope.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Measure whether endemic species from different islands in each archipelago are phylogenetically closer to one another than to species elsewhere, using clade-specific trees and null models. Consistent within-archipelago clustering confirms the empirical prediction.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Polyphyletic colonization can occur within an archipelago.", "Sequence coverage is sparse for many endemic invertebrates and plants.";
